<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Weert</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Weert is a town in the province of Limburg in the south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, near the Belgian border. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the main town of the County of Horne, whose counts held a castle there; Philip de Montmorency, Count of Horne, beheaded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> in 1568, was its most famous lord. Today it is a regional market and industrial town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/weert.jpg" alt="Weert" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Massimo Catarinella · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MartinuskerkWeertLimburgNederland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
